  },
  {
   "where": "LS-17 (L224), the dormancy sentence",
   "issue": "The inserted ADR-0012 sentences split the original 'on load M19 also advances ...; then it sets `dormant_since_step` to 0'. The text now reads 'M19 is callable under INIT ..., where it stamps `dormant_since` with the INIT step_no; then it sets `dormant_since_step` to 0'. The natural reading is that the INIT unload stamps the step and immediately zeroes it. That would make the next load's advance `step_no − 0`, so every absolute stamp jumps by the whole session length. The text also names the field both `dormant_since` and `dormant_since_step`.",
   "fix": "Move the 'then it sets `dormant_since_step` to 0' clause back to directly follow the load-time advance list. Put the INIT sentence after it as a separate clause. Use `dormant_since_step` throughout."
  }
